  "scope": "Stage4J5: D3D9 declaration/VS/PS live binding references are private storage holds. Public zero transitions manage exactly one device pin; common shader QueryInterface also revives it. Storage unlinks and frees metadata/code before the last device release. FVF, explicit unbind and Reset share private release. Recording and completed stateblocks retain prior public holds pending4J6. Native actual methods use constructor/emitter stubs:179968 checks,1024 final-owner profiles,24576 public-zero QI revivals,30 strictly compiled assertion mutants,two old actual setter/QI controls and ASAN/UBSAN. XP creates two declarations and two shaders per stage;384 QI revivals,384 getters and129 exact metadata rounds; four programmable UP draws, FVF retirement, explicit shader replacement, one successful Reset retaining external public objects and another successful binding-only Reset. Five simulated XP pixel replies prove transport only; dual GPU independently checks320 real pixels and all six accurate storage destructions before owner release. Cache hints preserve the existing guest/host limb-hash ABI; shader translation/hash algorithms are unchanged. D3D8,stateblock private holds,general external-child root-state retention,arbitrary callbacks/thread/loss/full Reset/format/MSAA/fullscreen/multi-buffer/wrapper conversion,native HAL,games/FPS and overall stages4/5/6 remain open. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/DDraw unchanged.",
